# Build and audit material that is not part of the release. Settled by the
# corresponding author on 4 October 2026, when this directory was first made a git
# repository, and recorded here rather than only in a commit message because a
# .gitignore is what the next person to clone actually reads.
#
#   snapshots/     33 build bundles, 60 of the package's 70 MB. REPRODUCIBILITY.md
#                  section 2 states that several of them contain claims this paper
#                  has since withdrawn and that nothing is quoted, reviewed or
#                  released from an old snapshot. Publishing them would contradict
#                  that sentence and hand a reader withdrawn claims.
#                  tools/snapshot.py still writes here and nothing reads the folder:
#                  the audit test reads snapshot.py's declarations, not the zips.
#   deliverables/  working documents about the paper -- audit records, the
#                  condensation spreadsheet, the problem-statement draft -- not
#                  parts of it.
#   pdf/           the built article and supplement. Both are reproducible from the
#                  tracked sources with tools/build_pdf.py, and publishing the
#                  article PDF is a preprint-posting question, separate from
#                  releasing the pipeline.
#
# None of the three is deleted. They stay in the working copy; they are simply not
# what is published.
snapshots/
deliverables/
pdf/

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are the release:
#   results/     the 750 per-fold rows, the registry, Arm A's probability files
#   figures/     the figures and figures/PROVENANCE.txt
#   manuscript/  the section files the manuscript is built from
# A .gitignore that swallowed any of those would turn a reproducible package back
# into a claim, which is the failure this repository exists to avoid.
